# Meta app

Requirements: Go 1.26.10+, Node.js/npm, and Air on PATH.

```sh
meta setup
meta dev
```

Create a `.env` file for local configuration. Values prefixed `VITE_` are public in the browser. Development uses `.env.local` over `.env`; production uses `.env.production` over `.env`. Shell variables take precedence. Restart after changing env files.

Open http://localhost:3000. Files in `public/` are available at the site root, such as `public/robots.txt` at `/robots.txt`. Tailwind CSS is configured in `frontend/app.css`; use utility classes in templ and Svelte files, or add your own global CSS there.

Configure server middleware and route policies in `app/hooks.go`. Policies do not provide authentication by themselves; implement your own credential and authorization checks.

To build a Node-free production server:

```sh
meta build
./bin/app
```

Run the binary from this project directory so it can find `dist/client`, `public`, and the optional `.env` and `.env.production` files.
